        <help>
		<line >Quick start  instructions (  No full autostart, sorry  )</line>
		<line>Master  Battery switch - ON ( Main Panel )</line>
		<line>Avionics master, 1 + 2 - ON  ( Overhead Panel )</line>
		<line>Prime pump 1+2 - ON  ( Overhead panel )</line>
		<line>Now use   the "Quick start".</line>
		<line>After Engines reach idle do the following:-</line>
 <line>XFER Pumps 1+2 - ON ( Overgead panel )</line>
 <line>Prime Pumps 1+2 - OFF ( Overhead panel )</line>
 <line>Set  both  twist grips to FLIGHT   mousing over + Mouse wheel. This is hard coded to the mouse, SORRY !</line>
 <line>All Warning indicators should be  OFF  on the screens.</line> 
            <line></line>
			<line>Full Manual start, not yet implemented </line>
			<line></line>
			<key>
              <name>}</name>
              <desc>Quick Start engines ( No Full autostart !! )</desc>
            </key>
           
                
            <key>
              <name>Ctrl d</name>
              <desc>Turn off SAS</desc>
            </key>
                      
          <key>
				<name>Q,Z,A,D</name>
				<desc>Rotate searchlight when fitted</desc>
			</key>
            <key>
              <name>r</name>
              <desc>Activate Winch Man ( see notes below )</desc>
            </key>
<line></line>
<line>For a full manual start use the checklist ether in sim or printable version. ( Not yet functional )</line>
<line></line>			
          <line>  Rotorbrake can only be activated by the lever on the cabin floor RHS of pilot seat.</line> 
            <line>All external lights are default to OFF</line>
            <line>  Landing light + Search light ( when fitted ) are switched on/off from the switches on the collective.</line>
            <line>  Search light ( when fitted ) needs to be armed first, via HISL sw. on overhead panel.</line>
            <line> All other exterior lights are controlled from the switches in the overhead panel.</line>
            <line> The winch man is only available on winch equipped payloads. He can only be seen when he has been activated and the sliding door is open..</line>
            <line></line>
            <line>Emergency Floatation system</line>
            <line> The system is currently available on SAY and Offshore payloads only.</line>
            <line>When fitted the arming switch is available on the overhead panel.</line>      
            <line>When armed the switch on the overhead will glow red. The red trigger switch will be available on the collective.</line>
        <line></line>
<line> SAR Menu option - THIS IS JUST A FUN MULTIPLAYER FEATURE !!</line>
			<line> If you crash your chopper, you can use this menu option to call on another EC145</line>
			<line>or any other chopper running the script, to retrieve your broken chopper and you, as an underslung load.</line>
<line> </line>
<line>AUTOPILOT V3 </line>
<line>The Autopilot is now able to control  speed, altitude and heading. Autopilot is only usable  between 30-140kts</line>
<line>Heading modes can be used without any other Autopilot function being active.</line>
<line>Speed modes can be used without any other Autopilot function being active.</line>
<line>****  Altitude modes can only be used in conjunction with speed mode being being active. This includes the use of Vertical Speed mode.  ***</line>
<line>AUTOPILOT ISSUES !!!!!</line>
<line>When disengaging the AP entirely or from a singe mode, the  control inputs will snap to your actual cyclic/colective/pedal positions as soon as you  move any of them.</line>
<line>This is unavoidable as  the sim can not physically move your cyclic/colective/pedal positions to match the Autopilots input.</line>
<line>The best advice to minimise the sudden change of input would be for you to  have your cyclic/colective/pedal positions ready in approximatly correct positions  to minimise the "snap".</line>

		
		</help>
		
